WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.270
April 7th, Torqyean Calendar Year 76.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.320
As the Balt-Rhein Empire's army sought to capture
the Republic of Chielo,

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.870
the Torqyean expeditionary force decided to engage
them in battle.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.040
The Torqyeans suffered thousands of losses

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.960
due to the Empire's new unconventional tactic.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.840
Sehir Halil Pasha, the Supreme Commander
of the expeditionary forces fell in battle.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.060
After seizing the Torqyean army's provisions,

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.990
the Empire makes it known to the besieged Chielo forces
that they are prepared for a war of attrition,

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.860
and the two sides are at a stalemate.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.030
Fearing the dwindling supplies within the castle,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.950
Tughril Mahmut Pasha requested relief
from their allies in Venedik.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:09.210
Doge Lucio set out with a fleet immediately.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.720
Targeting the blockade between Tharros and Phoinike

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.720
held by the Republic of L'isolani's Boccanegra Armada
at the Empire's request,

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.020
the Venedik Armada managed
to successfully break the blockade

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.600
after a great battle.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:33.780
Your mistake was to side with an empire
that knows nothing of the sea.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.490
As the last head of the Boccanegra family,

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.620
it's likely your name will be remembered.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.450
Farewell, Amadeo.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.300
Was this really the right decision?

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:04.680
The Boccanegras and the D'Orias have competed
over the Dogeship for generations.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.810
And he was especially rash.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.650
He simply bet on the wrong horse.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.690
And I didn't.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.740
There is no greater virtue than honesty.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.950
L'isolani is an ocean nation like yours.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.870
No matter how long the Empire
continues to succeed on land,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.880
we must never lose on water.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:37.340
In any case, L'isolani now openly
belongs to the D'Oria family.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.300
It's time to lay low

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:44.850
and wait for the next opportunity to determine
the Centro's next ruler.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.060
No, L'isolani's Golden Age has just ended.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.770
You will never get another opportunity.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.910
May 18th, Torqyean Calendar Year 76.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.830
The Empire lost its hold of the Centro,

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.990
and the surrounding 11 city-states

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.580
declared their opposition of the Empire's intervention.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.330
Venedik had won.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.760
This occurred a mere three days voyage from Chielo,

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.680
but it took over a month before
the news would reach them.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.140
An unseasonal storm blowing from
the Western Centro,

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.350
would hinder the Venedik Armada,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:38.190
and greatly impact the future of Chielo.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.570
Alliance Against the Empire

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:57.130
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:21.170
A Month Later
June 18th, Torqyean Calendar Year 76

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.130
The weather is finally going to clear up.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.140
That was a long storm.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.270
Are you really going, Pasha?

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.730
Yes, this is the only way to make it outside these walls
without being detected by the Empire's surveillance.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.360
You could just let him do it.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.700
But I suppose your mind's made up already.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.030
Padrone.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.790
Please remember the breathing technique I taught you.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.040
Take care of things while I'm gone.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.170
Carbajal, I can't do this anymore.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.010
The Venedik reinforcements
the Torqyean Pasha requested

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.220
should've been here by now.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.350
Venedik is the heartless country that left Phoinike to die.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.220
Now they've also betrayed us!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.520
There's also a chance they lost to the Empire at sea.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.560
Our wheat stores are almost out

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.770
because we took in the refugees.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.570
And the month-long rain has made so many sick,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.570
leaving us short on medicine.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.200
This is all because we couldn't eradicate
the Imperial army with our fire trap.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:35.950
Yeah! And on top of that, the Torqyean army lost their
commander when they're supposed to be our saviors!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.290
What is Mahmut Pasha doing?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.710
The Pasha...

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:46.380
Mahmut Pasha has gone to rally
the surviving Torqyean soldiers.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.590
We have to trust him and wait.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.720
Director...

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.860
Nobody move!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.400
Director, I'm sorry.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.530
We can't trust anything you say anymore.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.840
The Imperial army currently stands at 57,000 soldiers.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.300
And we don't even have 15,000.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.340
Despite your loss,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.140
I am grateful you were able to gather
so many surviving soldiers and remain in the area.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.520
We couldn't turn tail and run

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.810
after we helplessly watched Halil Pasha get killed.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.830
Then let us go.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:09.590
Chielo's fate depends on us.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.640
Let's see. Two, three...

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.390
Oh, did you see that?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.150
Iskandar circled three times!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.770
It seems the Padrone has finally
finished his preparations.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.240
Hey, we got real trouble!

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.530
Some of the militia unhappy with the siege

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.280
just captured Director Carbajal.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.870
They're planning on handing over the Director

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.500
and surrendering to the Empire!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.540
Open the gate!

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.750
8th Division, move out!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.300
Relieve the 6th Division stationed at Briar Gate.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.720
It's been two months since we started our siege.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.970
Because they took in the surrounding refugees,

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.100
I've heard the population in the castle exceeds 60,000.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.020
It seems Chielo's storehouses are bottomless.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.360
No, they're already at their limits.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.980
Whether they surrender or attack,

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.280
they're bound to take some action soon.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.410
Caution the troops to be on their guard.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.820
Wow.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.240
I think I'll start calling you the Prophet from now on.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.000
What are you talking about?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.500
You're being...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.670
Torqyean cavalry!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.390
They waited for our routine rotations.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.350
Are they looking to take down each division?

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.060
If they would rather die than surrender,

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.690
then I shall oblige.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.190
Move back the oxcarts!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.690
Form up with our main encampment's canal behind!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.110
We will take this fight!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.620
Charge!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.540
Horse archers, fire!

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.160
Ruckenschild!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.340
There is no artistry.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.260
How unimaginative.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.390
Iskandar!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.900
I see the cows!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.770
Aim for them! But don't kill them.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.410
The 8th Division's formation has been broken!

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.370
Send out the 3rd Division! Hurry!

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.110
-The sheep!
-What is going on?

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.200
Look! They're charging right at us!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.450
Close the gate! Close the gate!

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.580
It's too late!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.620
What are you doing, you fools!

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.420
Don't break formation!

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.550
It's a Torqyean horseman!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.800
This is bad, they're taking the sheep with them!

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.890
We did it, Mahmut Pasha!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.720
Good. That's enough.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.020
We're pulling back.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.690
My apologies, general.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.940
We've lost valuable food provisions and soldiers.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.490
To think their aim was to take back their food.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.360
We were outwitted.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.070
Being cut off from our supply line,

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.700
this was much more damaging
than losing thousands of soldiers.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.460
An impressive showing from an equestrian tribe.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:16.040
They know how to control sheep and cows.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.630
It's a tactic we won't be able to emulate.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.630
In the 76 years of Torqye's history,

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.260
no other Pasha has ever employed such a tactic.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.600
What was their commanding officer like?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.140
He was a blonde...

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.150
and young golden eagle handler.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.530
Golden eagle handler...

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:46.660
We did it! We got our livestock back.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.370
While a huge, stationary army is easily defendable,

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.200
the Empire will be forced to move now!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.000
Let's tear them to pieces

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.960
with our claws and fangs.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.930
June 20, Torqyean Calendar Year 76
Before Dawn

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.430
There they are, Julio.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.890
They're the Imperial soldiers sieging the Haubia Gate.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.680
Do you think this will work, Albano?

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:16.350
We've killed over 10,000 Imperial soldiers.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.360
Do you think giving this letter of surrender will work?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.900
That's why we're prepared to hand over the director.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.030
We just have to take that gamble.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.920
My employer is about to do something big.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.630
I'd hate for you to interfere.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.010
Hand over the flag of surrender.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.180
We need to show the Imperial army that we surrender.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.680
Where did you come from?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.360
I never get tired of watching him work.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.490
Thank you for your help, Kiros.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.620
Take a look at that, Abiriga.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.460
Ten thousand. Twenty thousand.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.130
My count puts them at nearly 42,000 soldiers.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:31.350
After their food has been stolen, they have no choice
but to move their main forces.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.760
Just as the Pasha drew up.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:38.270
And we can't mess things up for him
after he left us in charge of looking after the place.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:44.110
I'm not letting my fun with Mahmut
end with something like this.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.030
We won't let them surrender.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.530
No.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.990
And we're going to rescue Director Carbajal.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.750
What do you think, Prophet Frentzen?

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:05.590
Ambushing Torqye and stealing their supplies
using Lady Kokoschka's map-reading skills.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:11.340
I doubt you actually believe that the same plan
we used two months ago will work again.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.890
Good question.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:16.970
It's her job to make sure we win regardless.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:25.230
My stomach has been hurting
ever since I got up this morning.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:29.490
But how exactly have the Torqyean soldiers
been able to remain here

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.820
without any provisions to sustain them?

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.450
That's the thing, Siebel.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.580
Apparently they massed together in the Espada territory
where they've also been camping out all this time!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.870
That can't be true!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:47.250
Are you saying a small town like that
was able to provide for over 10,000 Torqyean soldiers?

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.970
Espada couldn't have done it alone.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.550
That's exactly right.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.680
Espada continued to receive goods from Cuore.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:04.770
It's surprising that the opportunistic Cuore
decided to side with the anti-Imperial alliance

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.570
amidst the Empire's rise to power.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:11.490
While we've been trying to starve out Chielo
for the last two months,

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.110
the entire eastern side of Rumeriana

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.450
has fallen in with the anti-Imperial alliance.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.500
It's only been four months since we began our invasion.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:25.290
The once-scattered Cuore
and small southern Rumeriana states

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.590
have unified into a functioning alliance.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.380
How were they able to do this?

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.550
I once asked Minister Louis that very question.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.970
He said that every time Torqye faces danger,

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.140
there is always a ray of hope that shines.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:45.060
That must be the blond golden eagle handler.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:49.020
Apparently he was Halil Pasha's foster child.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.530
Son of Halil.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.280
I never imagined I would meet him in this manner.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.160
Four Days Later
June 24, Torqyean Calendar Year 76

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.120
Let us go.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.730
We will circumvent the mountain

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.650
and head to the Murmullo Basin.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.820
So by the time we reach the basin...

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.490
Yes, it will be the night of a full moon.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:37.780
It's a little draining that we
are always marching during the night.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.580
The sheep seem happy though.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.910
Summer is mating season after all.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.460
They are more energetic at night this time of year.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.170
Five hundred years ago,
I'm sure our ancestors

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.800
shared a similar experience to this one.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.550
They say that a Torqyean march

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:03.100
was originally done at the behest of the sheep.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.060
Two Days Later
June 26, Torqyean Calendar Year 76

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:13.280
The Torqyean army will arrive at a basin
near the Espadan border in two nights.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.740
Night again?

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:18.030
They sneak around in the dark like rats!

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:22.280
They're likely being cautious after their previous defeat.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.540
They are only moving at night.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.710
And they've been deliberately avoiding
any routes near the river

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.920
to ensure we can't catch up to them using rafts.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.590
General Pino.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.960
Instead of focusing on the running Torqyeans,

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:40.800
wouldn't it better if we attacked the nations
with plenty of food like Espada and Humo

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.510
who have sided with the anti-Imperials?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.060
While putting Chielo at our backs is worrisome,

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.690
we could leave them to Frentzen and the others.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.310
Lord Kirchherr,

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.650
is it your wish to let this victory slip
through our fingers?

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.610
Why do you think we broke from the main camp

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.740
to pursue Torqye with such a large force?

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:04.080
Two nights from now is the spring tide.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:09.040
There is no better opportunity
to settle our score with Torqye.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:15.250
This anti-Imperial alliance will crumble
as soon as the Torqyean army is eradicated.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.300
Two Days Later
June 28, Torqyean Calendar Year 76

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.960
The river is overflowing.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.590
What an unsettling scene.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.300
The majority of the Murmullo Basin
is surrounded by rich grasslands.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:07.350
But there are several areas where no plants grow.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.730
Do you know why?

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:12.980
The area is at sea level.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.980
It's because every two weeks during the spring tide,

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:19.190
the land is ruined by sea water.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.450
We may have let them get away two months ago,

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.120
but that isn't going to happen this time.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.000
This is truly commendable.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.090
Not once, but twice now.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:43.550
This is just like when Halil Pasha fell.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.260
His strength is also his weakness.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:52.020
The march with the sheep that made Torqye the rulers
of Rumeriana 500 years ago

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.520
will be their downfall this time.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.360
The enemy troops have all stepped off their rafts?

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.360
Iskandar!

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.030
-What is it?
-Troops on the opposite shore!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.620
It's a sword emblem!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.870
It's the Espada army! Nearly 3000 soldiers!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.830
Anti-Imperials?

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.290
And from the hill behind!

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.920
It's the Humo and Seallant armies!

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.960
They total nearly 2000!

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.170
From the left too, Lady Kokoschka!

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:25.680
Impossible.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.100
What a beautiful sight, Derecho.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.930
Indeed, Izquierda.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.140
It's time to get revenge for Halil Pasha.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.060
Take down the Imperial army!

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:40.360
It's the bull emblem!
I count 5000 El Toro mercenaries!

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:42.480
The enemy is nearly 25,000 strong.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.360
We may have the numbers advantage,

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.320
but we have been completely surrounded!

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:51.080
It seems we fell right into their trap.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.160
It was not I, but Torqye

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:59.790
who decided on this place and time to make battle.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:07.010
I am no longer

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.970
a powerless child.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:52.660
Halil Pasha, it seems your death
gave birth to a new Pasha.

00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:56.240
A strong, young Pasha not held captive by revenge.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:59.040
Next time, "Golden Eagle's Pursuit."

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:00.540
Hoist the flag!
